scantly.d:
adv. In a scant manner; not fully or sufficiently; narrowly;
   penuriously.
adv. Scarcely; hardly; barely.

scragged.d:
a. Rough with irregular points, or a broken surface;
   scraggy; as, a scragged backbone.
a. Lean and rough; scraggy.

selenious.d:
a. Of, pertaining to, or containing, selenium;
   specifically, designating those compounds in which the element has a
   lower valence as contrasted with selenic compounds.
